<http://www.spektrix.com/artspring/event/38201AHNBNPJGLCLVNBPRCDPTCCSQSKKV> a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Cosi Fan Tutte (Mozart) (Met Opera)";
  schema:description """
	The Met: Live in HD opera season kicks off with one of Wolfgang Amadeus Mozart’s most sublime creations. Phelim McDermott’s “colorful, inventive” (The New York Times) staging of this satirical comedy of fickle young love is inspired by Coney Island in the 1950s - and sets the uproarious story at a boardwalk amusement park, where the two pairs of lovers at the heart of the tale find themselves on one emotional—and literal—thrill ride after another.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Soprano Federica Lombardi and mezzo-soprano Samantha Hankey sing Fiordiligi and Dorabella, opposite tenor Duke Kim and baritone Andrey Zhilikhovsky as Ferrando and Guglielmo. Bass-baritone Gerald Finley stars as the cynical Don Alfonso, with soprano Ana María Martínez as the witty maid Despina. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>This live cinema transmission is part of The Met: Live in HD series, bringing opera to movie theaters across the globe. Here at ArtSpring, enjoy our surround sound and famous quiche brunch during the intermission.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Performed in Italian with English subtitles <span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-10-03T10:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
