<http://www.spektrix.com/artspring/event/38601APMJBSGHLBVKJDHHGBQTTKBBSMSJ> a schema:Event;
  schema:name "Silent Night (Puts) (Met Opera)";
  schema:description """
	Composer Kevin Puts returns to the Met with his Pulitzer Prize-winning first opera. This evocative performance is inspired by the true events of the 1914 Christmas truce, when soldiers spontaneously set aside the horrors of the First World War and crossed the trenches to mingle, exchange gifts, and sing carols with the enemy. A poignant depiction of shared humanity in the most inhumane circumstances, Puts’s grand, cinematic opera—with a libretto by Mark Campbell based on the film Joyeux Noël—has been widely acclaimed since its 2011 premiere, hailed as “an overwhelming emotive experience” by The Guardian. The star-studded cast, featuring soprano Elza van den Heever and tenors Ben Bliss and Rolando Villazón, among many others, is conducted by debuting maestro Dalia Stasevska. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>This live cinema transmission is part of The Met: Live in HD series, bringing opera to movie theaters across the globe. Here at ArtSpring, enjoy our surround sound and famous quiche brunch during the intermission.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Performed in English, French, German, Italian and Latin with English subtitles<span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2027-03-20T10:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/artspring/files/739464f6-9fe1-4978-abcc-a41534acdb23.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/artspring/location/403ASKCQMVCSKPPLNQMQPJVVSRPGMSKLR>;
