<http://www.spektrix.com/artspring/event/35402AKGBQBNDMNKSNVCHHKDHMPQJTDHK> a schema:Event;
  schema:name "SS Baroque: Ensemble Il Postiglione";
  schema:description """
	At Fulford Hall<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Ensemble Il Postiglione takes its name from the postiglione - the stagecoach rider who signalled each arrival with a bright octave leap on the post horn, a gesture that Baroque composers loved to echo in their music. That same spirited interval appears in Telemann’s Il Postiglione Sonata, a nod to the lively, travelling-world energy that inspires the ensemble’s identity.<span><br/></span>Founded in Europe by harpsichordist Simone Pierini and recorder/traverso virtuoso Romeo Ciuffa, the ensemble has since performed across the globe. For this concert, they are joined by violinists Enrique Gómez‑Cabrero Fernández and Paul Luchkow, and soprano Anne Grimm.  They will be performing on exquisite 17th‑century period instruments, including a single‑register harpsichord crafted by Fabrizio Acanfora in Barcelona.  These world-class musicians have come together on Salt Spring to participate in Salt Spring Baroque's opera Acis and Galatea, and we are thrilled to have them perform this concert while they are here.
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-08-19T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/artspring/files/24bb7a9f-2431-4bdb-b609-a47424cad213.jpeg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/artspring/location/402AJKCLLRDNMBKMHTCGLBDHJTBPJBDNV>;
  schema:duration "PT120M";
  schema:endDate "2026-08-19T21:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

<https://spektrix.com/artspring/location/402AJKCLLRDNMBKMHTCGLBDHJTBPJBDNV> a schema:Place;
  schema:name "Fulford Hall" .

<http://www.spektrix.com/artspring/event/35401APNVLPNRJRDCGRRCTSSJTSMNRNQD> a schema:Event;
  schema:name "SS Baroque: Handel's ACIS AND GALATEA Baroque Opera";
  schema:description """
	At Fulford Hall<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Experience Salt Spring’s first-ever baroque opera!<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Salt Spring Baroque is thrilled to present George Frideric Handel's masterpiece, Acis and Galatea, under the direction of renowned Spanish violinist and conductor Enrique Gómez-Cabrero Fernández.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Adapted from Ovid’s Metamorphoses, this beloved English-language opera weaves a captivating tale of doomed love, sensuality, humour, and pastoral tragedy. Follow the romance between the nymph Galatea and the shepherd Acis, and the jealous giant Polyphemus, who threatens to tear them apart.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Brought to life by a brilliant baroque orchestra playing on period instruments, incredible vocal soloists, and a chorus of your own Salt Spring friends and neighbours, this performance features the full, magnificent 1718 version of Handel's work.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Whether you are a lifelong classical music lover or experiencing baroque opera for the very first time, this is an extraordinary community event you won’t want to miss!
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-08-22T14:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/artspring/files/75411a2b-cf19-41b9-8ba0-4040bd3be9f6.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/artspring/location/402AJKCLLRDNMBKMHTCGLBDHJTBPJBDNV>;
  schema:offers _:6cfb468278f340539e63131aadaca0c98361;
  schema:duration "PT120M";
  schema:endDate "2026-08-22T16:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

