<http://www.spektrix.com/artspring/event/37201ANNHRQCTNHTBVHBGGJGJCBQDGBJG> a schema:Event;
  schema:name "SS Forum Presents Arno Kopecky: What Went Wrong With the Climate Crisis Response?";
  schema:description """
	Can we take meaningful action on climate change without damaging our economy?<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>For more than two decades, journalist and author Arno Kopecky has examined the difficult trade-offs that define our relationship with nature. Kopecky has travelled the globe reporting from the front lines of environmental change, asking uncomfortable questions about conservation, climate change, Indigenous rights, and energy. Rather than offering easy answers, he challenges us to think more deeply about what it really means to live sustainably. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Arno Kopecky is an award-winning journalist whose work has appeared in The Globe and Mail, Maclean’s, The Guardian, The Narwhal, The Tyee, and many other publications. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Please join the Salt Spring Forum in welcoming Arno Kopecky for the 2nd annual Derek Lundy Memorial Event, where we will discuss the complex political and ethical dilemmas raised by a global ecological crisis.
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-09-26T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/artspring/files/759303f6-b4d5-4ef6-9c1c-a9eae7e6a475.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/artspring/location/403ASKCQMVCSKPPLNQMQPJVVSRPGMSKLR>;
  schema:offers _:6cfb468278f340539e63131aadaca0c98378;
  schema:duration "PT90M";
  schema:endDate "2026-09-26T21:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

