<http://www.spektrix.com/artspring/event/35001ANDBMVNTNMQTQBCTTLTMVTJHVKBV> a schema:Event;
  schema:name "SS Forum: Adam Olsen: Who's Afraid of DRIPA";
  schema:description """
	Crown-Indigenous relations in British Columbia have been badly strained since the BC Supreme Court found, last August, that the Cowichan Nation holds Aboriginal title to a portion of land in Richmond. Some politicians and pundits seized on the Court decision to argue that private property was at risk. But is private property really at risk? What do the legislation and court judgments actually say? Why have these matters become so politicized? <span><br/></span>Adam Olsen is perfectly positioned to answer these and other questions. When Adam steps up to speak, he brings more than political experience – he carries age-old stories shaped by land, law and leadership. A proud member of the Tsartlip First Nation and former MLA for Saanich North and the Islands, Adam has spent years at the intersection of Indigenous governance and provincial decision-making. Please join the Forum and Adam Olsen for this compelling discussion.
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-06-21T19:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/artspring/files/c64cd202-2923-4193-bb71-74ddfa465f87.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/artspring/location/403ASKCQMVCSKPPLNQMQPJVVSRPGMSKLR>;
  schema:offers _:6cfb468278f340539e63131aadaca0c98381;
  schema:duration "PT90M";
  schema:endDate "2026-06-21T21:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

_:6cfb468278f340539e63131aadaca0c98381 a schema:AggregateOffer;
  schema:url <https://tickets.artspring.ca/Online/default.asp?doWork::WScontent::loadArticle=Load&BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::article_id=31601>;
  schema:lowPrice "0.0";
  schema:priceCurrency "CAD" .

<http://www.spektrix.com/artspring/event/44401ADDCBDNQTQBKSGKTVMSVMQDMMLLG> a schema:Event;
  schema:name "SS Forum: Coalter Lathrop";
  schema:description """
	The deepest reaches of our oceans are among the least explored places on Earth. Yet they have become the location of an international race for essential minerals. As governments and corporations push to mine the deep seabed, a fundamental question has emerged: Who will determine the fate of the world’s oceans?<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>For Coalter Lathrop, that question is not just about the oceans—it’s about the future of the international order itself.<span><br/></span>A world-leading international lawyer and marine cartographer, Lathrop advises governments and international organizations on the world’s most complex ocean and territorial disputes. He is the perfect person to help us understand the complex dynamics involved in the current conflict over seabed resources. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span>For many of us who live beside the Pacific Ocean, this issue is deeply personal. It’s about the future of our shared planet—and whether the rules that have governed our oceans for generations can withstand the pressures of a fast-changing world.
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-12-06T15:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/artspring/files/3df9147b-004c-4e83-a623-85be6406d231.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/artspring/location/403ASKCQMVCSKPPLNQMQPJVVSRPGMSKLR>;
  schema:offers _:6cfb468278f340539e63131aadaca0c98382;
  schema:duration "PT90M";
  schema:endDate "2026-12-06T16:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

_:6cfb468278f340539e63131aadaca0c98382 a schema:AggregateOffer;
  schema:url <https://tickets.artspring.ca/Online/default.asp?doWork::WScontent::loadArticle=Load&BOparam::WScontent::loadArticle::article_id=40201>;
