<http://www.spektrix.com/artspring/event/44201ABVSPQTRSSSNTBJLJHTGPNHBHBLM> a schema:Event;
  schema:name "SS Forum: Jason Kenney";
  schema:description """
	Canada has always been a country of competing identities, regional priorities, and political differences. But today, these tensions feel stronger than before. Many Canadians are asking a difficult question: What holds us together—and what could pull us apart?<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Few people have been closer to these debates than Jason Kenney. A former Premier of Alberta and federal cabinet minister with portfolios over immigration, employment, and defence, Kenney has spent more than 25 years at the centre of Canadian politics. He has shaped national immigration policy, negotiated intergovernmental relationships, and led Canada’s most resource-dependent province through periods of profound economic and political change.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span>Some Salt Spring Islanders will disagree with Jason Kenney’s politics. But agree with him or not, this is a rare opportunity to hear directly from one of Canada’s most influential conservative voices about one of the most important questions: Where does Canada go from here?
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-11-15T15:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/artspring/files/f9279733-3bca-4cb7-8c10-d7a4c6f4c23a.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/artspring/location/403ASKCQMVCSKPPLNQMQPJVVSRPGMSKLR>;
  schema:offers _:6cfb468278f340539e63131aadaca0c98384;
  schema:duration "PT90M";
  schema:endDate "2026-11-15T16:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

