<http://www.spektrix.com/artspring/event/40201AJMHGMLBHTGVNKHNPGVSVHHPSMBQ> a schema:Event;
  schema:name "TULUA (AP)";
  schema:description """
	Young but traditional—Tulua have been described by the Irish Independent as “one of the hottest young prospects in traditional Irish music”. Hailing from the south east of Ireland, Tulua successfully toured Canada in 2025—including as official showcase artists at the 2025 Folk Alliance International Conference in Montreal—and are now bringing their second album to our shores. Meaning ‘tribe of many paths’ Tulua have been deeply exploring and sharing music of their local area and other parts of Ireland, bringing the audience with them on a captivating journey of songs about love, tunes about life, and everything in between. Their passion for playing music has evolved together from a young age, and they combine their core of fiddles, voice, flute, guitar and piano with a host of other instruments. Expect a toe-tapping, fresh and fun evening of music that fills the theatre with energy and joy. <span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Thank you to the Reinette Foundation, and Alison and Paul McManus, for sponsoring this performance.</span><span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2026-11-01T14:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
