<http://www.spektrix.com/artspring/event/41801AVTMRHQTMCCLMJSHHVVQTNHJPGQB> a schema:Event;
  schema:name "YUKI THE JUGGLER (AP)";
  schema:description """
	From samurai swords to crystal ball manipulation, this family-friendly performance combines skill with cultural exchange. All the Way From Japan blends traditional Japanese artistry with modern circus skills, in a dynamic fusion of Edo Daikagura—an over 400-year-old performance tradition—alongside cutting-edge juggling and comedic audience interaction. Rooted in celebration, ritual, and good fortune, Edo Daikagura brings symbolic meaning to every movement: spinning objects evoke harmony and continuity, while intricate balancing feats represent stability and perseverance. Yuki brings rare, lineage-based knowledge to the stage, having trained in Bunkyo, Tokyo under the 13th-generation master of the prestigious Maruichi Senoh Troupe—offering audiences an authentic glimpse into an art form with fewer than 150 active practitioners remaining in Japan. Be part of an experience that not only entertains, but preserves and shares this vanishing art form.<span><br/></span><span><br/></span><span class=\"ItalicText\">Thank you to Mouat’s Home Hardware for sponsoring this performance.</span><span><br/></span>
""";
  schema:startDate "2027-02-13T14:30:00"^^xsd:dateTime;
  schema:image <https://system.spektrix.com/artspring/files/9cbcf417-5b18-484c-bbd9-d5d086599273.jpg>;
  schema:location <https://spektrix.com/artspring/location/403ASKCQMVCSKPPLNQMQPJVVSRPGMSKLR>;
  schema:offers _:6cfb468278f340539e63131aadaca0c98445;
  schema:duration "PT90M";
  schema:endDate "2027-02-13T16:00:00"^^xsd:dateTime .

